1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,604
GPS satellites have no idea where you are.

2
00:00:03,734 --> 00:00:05,285
Your phone sends them nothing:

3
00:00:05,285 --> 00:00:06,292
it just listens.

4
00:00:06,422 --> 00:00:08,956
Above you, twenty thousand kilometers up,

5
00:00:08,956 --> 00:00:10,961
fly more than thirty satellites.

6
00:00:11,091 --> 00:00:12,642
Each one repeats two things:

7
00:00:12,642 --> 00:00:14,812
where it is and what time it is.

8
00:00:14,942 --> 00:00:17,102
The signal travels at the speed of light:

9
00:00:17,102 --> 00:00:19,754
it arrives in about seventy milliseconds.

10
00:00:19,884 --> 00:00:22,693
From that delay, your phone works out the distance.

11
00:00:22,823 --> 00:00:25,234
One satellite puts you on a circle.

12
00:00:25,364 --> 00:00:27,331
Three circles cross at a single point.

13
00:00:27,461 --> 00:00:29,225
The fourth corrects your phone's clock.

14
00:00:29,355 --> 00:00:30,648
One absurd detail:

15
00:00:30,648 --> 00:00:32,387
up there, time runs faster,

16
00:00:32,387 --> 00:00:34,853
by thirty-eight millionths of a second a day.

17
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:37,246
It sounds like nothing, but at the speed of

18
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:40,063
light that's about ten kilometers of error per day.

19
00:00:40,193 --> 00:00:43,602
That's why satellite clocks are corrected with Einstein's equations.

20
00:00:43,732 --> 00:00:46,346
Comment GPS and I'll send you the sources.
